[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] Define the shared, versioned content-package schema, read-only registry, and
[stderr] validator that reject malformed or internally inconsistent content before it
[stderr] can be loaded for play. The contract validates structure and relationships;
[stderr] it does not author a town, dungeon, dialogue, map, encounter, or other campaign
[stderr] expression.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Dependencies
[stderr] 
[stderr] R0001 provides the project boundary, R0003 provides deterministic fixtures,
[stderr] and R0004 provides versioned campaign-state envelopes. They are implementation
[stderr] dependencies, not authoring blockers. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003: save storage
[stderr] API, quota, support-window, and recovery policy decisions remain owned by the
[stderr] local-save protocol. This content contract neither chooses nor writes a save or
[stderr] cache implementation.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Ownership
[stderr] 
[stderr] - `src/content/{schema,validator,registry}/`.
[stderr] - `tests/content/validation.*` and deterministic content graph fixtures.
[stderr] - `docs/content-authoring.md`.
[stderr] - The versioned content-package, asset/provenance-manifest, and validator API
[stderr]   contracts.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The content registry loads only a fully validated package and is read-only at
[stderr] runtime. It does not own campaign state, save snapshots, preferences, browser
[stderr] storage, PWA cache records, migrations, assets, or release packaging.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Required behaviour
[stderr] 
[stderr] Model a package with stable package ID, semantic version, schema version,
[stderr] default locale, scenes, exits, dialogues, quests, encounters, enemy and item
[stderr] definitions, rewards, localisation, and an asset/provenance manifest. Validate
[stderr] before registry publication: schema shape and bounded input, required fields,
[stderr] unique stable IDs, locale-key and asset/provenance references, predicates,
[stderr] scene/spawn/exit targets, reward/item/enemy references, duplicate reward IDs,
[stderr] safe quest-item removal paths, and a reachable opening-to-ending path.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Validation must return typed diagnostics and must not partially register an
[stderr] invalid package. Build-time content import runs through this validator; derived
[stderr] bundles are never hand edited. Runtime discovery of a bad package stops the
[stderr] affected route, retains existing campaign/save data, and offers title or retry
[stderr] rather than mutating or replacing state.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Content compatibility is declared explicitly so the save/recovery owner can
[stderr] compare a snapshot's content package/version without making the content
[stderr] registry a persistence driver. Do not checkpoint, promote, overwrite,
[stderr] quarantine, migrate, or delete a save here; those operations remain gated under
[stderr] GATE-0003 and belong to R0006 and later R0007.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] 
[stderr] Web and PWA use the same shared validator, schema, and read-only registry. A
[stderr] PWA cache is a delivery concern, not a content-validation result or save store;
[stderr] neither target may bypass validation, write the active package at runtime, or
[stderr] conflate cache failure with save recovery.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Non-goals
[stderr] 
[stderr] Do not create authored campaign content, dialogue, maps, art, audio, sprites,
[stderr] icons, localisation copy, release bundles, gameplay algorithms, UI flows,
[stderr] browser/PWA cache lifecycle, save drivers, migrations, export/import, cloud
[stderr] sync, accounts, network clients, or storage policy. Do not resolve GATE-0003
[stderr] or GATE-0004; content quantities, locales, and detail remain unapproved.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Asset assessment
[stderr] 
[stderr] `asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this work defines schemas and validation
[stderr] only. Do not create, reserve, source, or generate incidental visual, audio,
[stderr] font, icon, illustration, texture, sprite, map, dialogue, or other product
[stderr] asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank. The schema may reserve fields for
[stderr] later original assets and provenance review without assigning an asset.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Verification
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Load a valid minimal package and prove publication succeeds only after all
[stderr]   validation phases complete.
[stderr] - Use one deterministic invalid fixture for each reference class: duplicate ID,
[stderr]   missing locale or asset/provenance record, invalid predicate, unresolved
[stderr]   scene/exit/reward/item/enemy reference, unsafe quest-item removal, and
[stderr]   unreachable ending; prove no invalid fixture is registered.
[stderr] - Traverse a valid fixture from opening scene to ending and prove required
[stderr]   transitions and rewards resolve.
[stderr] - Verify a runtime-invalid-package result retains the existing state/save and
[stderr]   provides title/retry recovery without selecting a storage API.
[stderr] - Before recording the B0004 checkpoint, validate the runbook loader parses
[stderr]   this front matter, provenance is non-empty and maps to IMP-0005, dependencies
[stderr]   match the manifest, owned paths are distinct from R0006, and every required
[stderr]   section is present. Stop on any mismatch; never overwrite an R contract.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Evidence
[stderr] 
[stderr] Retain validator output for the valid package and every rejected reference
[stderr] class, reachability traversal output, registry non-publication assertions,
[stderr] runtime title/retry recovery evidence, and the pre-checkpoint loader,
[stderr] provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation record.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] 
[stderr] - A valid minimal versioned package is the only kind of package the read-only
[stderr]   registry can publish.
[stderr] - Invalid IDs, references, predicates, localisation/provenance links, unsafe
[stderr]   quest-item removal paths, and unreachable campaign graphs fail before play.
[stderr] - Content/save compatibility is explicit while save, cache, migration, and
[stderr]   storage decisions remain separate and GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 remains retained.
[stderr] 
