[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] After DEC-0001 selects the framework, package manager, and CI baseline, create
[stderr] the smallest reproducible project skeleton for the shared game core, web
[stderr] adapter, and PWA adapter. Document one bootstrap, format, lint, and
[stderr] deterministic test command interface, and make a clean approved-runtime
[stderr] checkout run a deterministic sample test. This task establishes boundaries and
[stderr] tooling only; it does not implement game behaviour or resolve the decision.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Dependencies
[stderr] 
[stderr] This is the first implementation contract and has no R-series dependencies.
[stderr] GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 is retained as a human implementation precondition:
[stderr] authoring this runbook does not select a stack, and implementation must stop
[stderr] before selecting or installing framework, package-manager, or CI tooling.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Ownership
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Root build and tooling configuration, including the pinned toolchain
[stderr]   declaration and command mapping.
[stderr] - `src/core/`, `src/content/`, `src/app/`, `src/platform/web/`, and
[stderr]   `src/platform/pwa/` ownership directories, created without feature code.
[stderr] - `tests/` and an isolated deterministic sample-test location.
[stderr] - `docs/development.md`, which records the approved-runtime bootstrap,
[stderr]   format, lint, and deterministic-test commands once DEC-0001 is decided.
[stderr] - The build/test command interface: `bootstrap`, `format`, `lint`, and
[stderr]   `test:deterministic` (or the selected tool's documented equivalent).
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Behaviour
[stderr] 
[stderr] Use the DEC-0001-approved runtime only. Pin its version and package-manager
[stderr] lock/metadata as appropriate to that approved selection. Create the isolated
[stderr] directory skeleton so later work has distinct shared-core, content, app,
[stderr] web-adapter, PWA-adapter, and test ownership.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Configure the selected tooling so the documented command interface has a
[stderr] single reproducible mapping for bootstrap, formatting, linting, and a
[stderr] deterministic sample test. The sample test must use no wall clock, network,
[stderr] player data, browser storage, renderer, or platform feature. Record the exact
[stderr] commands and a clean-checkout result in `docs/development.md`.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The skeleton must preserve the canonical direction: target adapters are
[stderr] separate from the shared deterministic core, and no directory implies that a
[stderr] target may change campaign rules. Later R0002 owns enforcement of detailed
[stderr] core/adapter dependency rules.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] 
[stderr] The responsive web and installable PWA targets receive separate adapter
[stderr] directories only. Neither adapter gains a renderer, service worker, cache
[stderr] lifecycle, browser API dependency, or target-specific campaign behaviour in
[stderr] this task. PWA installation, caching, offline delivery, and update activation
[stderr] remain later scoped work; the PWA directory is an ownership boundary, not an
[stderr] implementation of those features.
[stderr] 
