",\"title\":\"Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0006\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0009\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; local redacted records only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"consent and deletion controls\",\"payload redaction\",\"no network transport\",\"GATE-0005 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and wait for privacy gate where required\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0010\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0010\",\"title\":\"Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0010\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No final artwork, fonts, or icons; semantic tokens only and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"non-colour cues\",\"reduced motion values\",\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and await numeric design decisions\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0011\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0011\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets are created; this contract defines provenance controls for later asset-required work.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"missing provenance rejected\",\"human creative review recorded\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0012\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\",\"R0006\",\"R0008\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0012\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0006\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"all foundation ownership/dependencies/gates cross-checked\",\"does not claim release readiness\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this documentation contract\"}\n  ]\n}\n---\ntask_id: R0005\nsequence: 5\ntitle: Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\ndependencies: R0001,R0003,R0004\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas,specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0005\nauthoring_batch: B0004\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No art or audio assets; reserve schema and provenance fields only for later original assets.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDefine the shared, versioned content-package schema, read-only registry, and\nvalidator that reject malformed or internally inconsistent content before it\ncan be loaded for play. The contract validates structure and relationships;\nit does not author a town, dungeon, dialogue, map, encounter, or other campaign\nexpression.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0001 provides the project boundary, R0003 provides deterministic fixtures,\nand R0004 provides versioned campaign-state envelopes. They are implementation\ndependencies, not authoring blockers. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003: save storage\nAPI, quota, support-window, and recovery policy decisions remain owned by the\nlocal-save protocol. This content contract neither chooses nor writes a save or\ncache implementation.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `src/content/{schema,validator,registry}/`.\n- `tests/content/validation.*` and deterministic content graph fixtures.\n- `docs/content-authoring.md`.\n- The versioned content-package, asset/provenance-manifest, and validator API\n  contracts.\n\nThe content registry loads only a fully validated package and is read-only at\nruntime. It does not own campaign state, save snapshots, preferences, browser\nstorage, PWA cache records, migrations, assets, or release packaging.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nModel a package with stable package ID, semantic version, schema version,\ndefault locale, scenes, exits, dialogues, quests, encounters, enemy and item\ndefinitions, rewards, localisation, and an asset/provenance manifest. Validate\nbefore registry publication: schema shape and bounded input, required fields,\nunique stable IDs, locale-key and asset/provenance references, predicates,\nscene/spawn/exit targets, reward/item/enemy references, duplicate reward IDs,\nsafe quest-item removal paths, and a reachable opening-to-ending path.\n\nValidation must return typed diagnostics and must not partially register an\ninvalid package. Build-time content import runs through this validator; derived\nbundles are never hand edited. Runtime discovery of a bad package stops the\naffected route, retains existing campaign/save data, and offers title or retry\nrather than mutating or replacing state.\n\nContent compatibility is declared explicitly so the save/recovery owner can\ncompare a snapshot's content package/version without making the content\nregistry a persistence driver. Do not checkpoint, promote, overwrite,\nquarantine, migrate, or delete a save here; those operations remain gated under\nGATE-0003 and belong to R0006 and later R0007.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nWeb and PWA use the same shared validator, schema, and read-only registry. A\nPWA cache is a delivery concern, not a content-validation result or save store;\nneither target may bypass validation, write the active package at runtime, or\nconflate cache failure with save recovery.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not create authored campaign content, dialogue, maps, art, audio, sprites,\nicons, localisation copy, release bundles, gameplay algorithms, UI flows,\nbrowser/PWA cache lifecycle, save drivers, migrations, export/import, cloud\nsync, accounts, network clients, or storage policy. Do not resolve GATE-0003\nor GATE-0004; content quantities, locales, and detail remain unapproved.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this work defines schemas and validation\nonly. Do not create, reserve, source, or generate incidental visual, audio,\nfont, icon, illustration, texture, sprite, map, dialogue, or other product\nasset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank. The schema may reserve fields for\nlater original assets and provenance review without assigning an asset.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Load a valid minimal package and prove publication succeeds only after all\n  validation phases complete.\n- Use one deterministic invalid fixture for each reference class: duplicate ID,\n  missing locale or asset/provenance record, invalid predicate, unresolved\n  scene/exit/reward/item/enemy reference, unsafe quest-item removal, and\n  unreachable ending; prove no invalid fixture is registered.\n- Traverse a valid fixture from opening scene to ending and prove required\n  transitions and rewards resolve.\n- Verify a runtime-invalid-package result retains the existing state/save and\n  provides title/retry recovery without selecting a storage API.\n- Before recording the B0004 checkpoint, validate the runbook loader parses\n  this front matter, provenance is non-empty and maps to IMP-0005, dependencies\n  match the manifest, owned paths are distinct from R0006, and every required\n  section is present. Stop on any mismatch; never overwrite an R contract.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain validator output for the valid package and every rejected reference\nclass, reachability traversal output, registry non-publication assertions,\nruntime title/retry recovery evidence, and the pre-checkpoint loader,\nprovenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation record.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A valid minimal versioned package is the only kind of package the read-only\n  registry can publish.\n- Invalid IDs, references, predicates, localisation/provenance links, unsafe\n  quest-item removal paths, and unreachable campaign graphs fail before play.\n- Content/save compatibility is explicit while save, cache, migration, and\n  storage decisions remain separate and GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 remains retained.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -C 4 'R0005|B0004|accepted|provenance' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/*.md runbooks/F014.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-42-## Checkpoint and update procedure\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-43-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-44-Atomically update the JSON/Markdown ledger counters, chapter state, contract\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-45-allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md:46:rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-47-dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-48-queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-49-B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-50-it must not pretend to generate or review all work in this dispatch.\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-52-## Validation procedure\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-53-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-54-Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-55-files, no more than seven assigned R IDs per B file, unique B/R/IMP IDs,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md:56:dependency closure, provenance val