nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md-66-## Collision protection\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md-67-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md-68-Before creating any B, R, IMP, successor, or audit path, verify that its ID and\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md-80-- The iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md-81-- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md-82-- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md-83-- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md:84:- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-1-# Runbook-authoring allocation ledger\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-2-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:3:This readable companion to [`runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](runbook-authoring-manifest.json) is the persistent allocation ledger for the mock-fantasy-quest-4 authoring system. The JSON is authoritative for IDs, provenance, dependencies, output paths, counters, and recovery state. Accepted IDs are immutable: resume from the first non-accepted batch and append only at `B0007` and `R0013`.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-4-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-5-## Dispatcher checkpoint \u2014 D0001\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-6-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-7-D0001 expanded no chapter and allocated no B/R contracts. `SHARD-02` is the\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-9-and `SHARD-04` retain their predecessor and gate blocks, while `SHARD-05` stays\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-10-held pending explicit authorisation. Every current catalogue contract\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-11-(`IMP-0001` through `IMP-0012`) is allocated exactly once. The dispatcher\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-12-therefore created [`D0002`](../authoring-runbooks/D0002.md) as the sole\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:13:successor, without advancing B/R counters or modifying accepted work.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-14-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-15-## Wave 1 \u2014 foundation contracts\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-16-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-17-| Order | Batch | R contracts (maximum 7) | Dependency / parallel disposition | Checkpoint |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-18-| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-19-| 1 | B0001 | R0001 | GATE-0001; no parallel work | Record gate and R0001 ownership |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-20-| 2 | B0002 | R0002, R0003, R0010 | After B0001 | Validate seams, fixtures, tokens and retained gates |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-21-| 3 | B0003 | R0004, R0008 | After B0002 | Validate state slice and P0 service exclusion |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:22:| 4 | B0004 | R0005, R0006 | After B0003; R0006 waits for GATE-0003 | Validate content/save separation |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:23:| 5 | B0005 | R0007, R0009, R0011 | After B0004; R0007/GATE-0003 and R0009/GATE-0005 remain blocked | Validate migration, diagnostics, provenance |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:24:| 6 | B0006 | R0012 | After B0003 and B0004; safe in parallel with B0005 after B0004 | Cross-check foundation documentation and gates |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-25-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:26:The batches are deliberately smaller than seven where a contract is context-heavy (state, persistence, content) or tightly coupled to its predecessor. Together they form an incremental foundation vertical slice: reproducible baseline, shared seams/test harness, deterministic game state and P0 exclusion, content and recovery boundaries, then provenance/diagnostic controls and documented closure. They do not imply that the game is implemented.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-27-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-28-## Contract allocation and asset assessment\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-29-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-30-| R ID | IMP source | Writer | Output | Asset assessment |\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-32-| R0001 | IMP-0001 | B0001 | `runbooks/R0001.md` | not applicable \u2014 tooling boundary only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-33-| R0002 | IMP-0002 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0002.md` | not applicable \u2014 interfaces only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-34-| R0003 | IMP-0003 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0003.md` | not applicable \u2014 deterministic fixtures only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-35-| R0004 | IMP-0004 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0004.md` | not applicable \u2014 state envelopes only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:36:| R0005 | IMP-0005 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0005.md` | not applicable \u2014 schema reserves later asset fields |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:37:| R0006 | IMP-0006 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0006.md` | not applicable \u2014 save/recovery protocol |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-38-| R0007 | IMP-0007 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0007.md` | not applicable \u2014 migrations only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-39-| R0008 | IMP-0008 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0008.md` | not applicable \u2014 negative service scope |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-40-| R0009 | IMP-0009 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0009.md` | not applicable \u2014 local diagnostics only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-41-| R0010 | IMP-0010 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0010.md` | not applicable \u2014 no final art/fonts/icons |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:42:| R0011 | IMP-0011 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0011.md` | not applicable \u2014 provenance control only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-43-| R0012 | IMP-0012 | B0006 | `runbooks/R0012.md` | not applicable \u2014 documentation only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-44-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-45-No Wave 1 contract creates a product asset. Each contract still carries an explicit `asset_impact`, empty `asset_ids`, and an asset brief in the JSON; its author must prohibit incidental asset creation. A later asset-required contract must reserve stable product-specific IDs and a brief before assignment.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-46-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-47-## Author packet and resume rules\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-48-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:49:Each B writer receives only the baseline terminology, target constraints, templates, authoring rules, and the named specification/catalogue records in its JSON `context_packet`. Every R record has canonical `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`, and `factory_stages` provenance. Use [`runbooks/TEMPLATE.md`](../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md) plus the F014 metadata and asset requirements.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-50-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:51:At every checkpoint, validate unique B/R IDs, output-path ownership, dependency closure, provenance, the batch maximum, asset assessment, and retained human gates. On failure, retain all assigned IDs, repair the bounded failed output, and resume that same batch. Never regenerate accepted contracts or renumber the ledger.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-52-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-53-## Queued expansion chapters\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-54-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-55-| Chapter | Future allocation point | State |\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-58-| SHARD-03 \u2014 Session, UI, input, and accessibility | Wave 3 after SHARD-02 and GATE-0002/0003/0004 | queued |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-59-| SHARD-04 \u2014 PWA delivery, performance, operations, release evidence | Wave 4 after SHARD-02/03 and GATE-0002/0005/0007 | queued |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-60-| SHARD-05 \u2014 Connected-scope decision package | Only explicit authorisation after GATE-0006; no P0 R allocation | hold |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-61-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:62:Expand one queued chapter into catalogue records before allocating its R IDs. This preserves the catalogue\u2019s dependency graph and makes a future thousand-runbook programme resumable without changing accepted work.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-63-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-64-## Structural check\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-65-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-66-```sh\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md-25-- `../runbooks/R0008.md` \u2014 IMP-0008; dependencies R0002,R0004.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md-26-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md-27-## Required authoring content\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md-28-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md:29:Use exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch: B0003`, standard\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md-30-Supervisor metadata, and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md-31-`asset_ids`. Each R file must include precise objective, dependencies,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md-32-requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md-33-differences, verification/evidence, observable accep