jects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-26-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-27-## Required authoring content\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-28-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md:29:Use standard front matter, exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch: B0004`),\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-30-and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank `asset_ids`. Each output must\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-31-cover objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership, behaviour, non-goals,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-32-platform differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-33-and an `## Asset assessment` forbidding incidental asset creation.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-34-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-35-## Validation procedure\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-36-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-37-Never overwrite a conflicting R file. Load and compare both files with the\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md:38:manifest, including provenance and dependencies, then verify required sections\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-39-and GATE-0003 retention.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-40-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-41-## Checkpoint and update procedure\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-42-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md:43:Update B0004 only after both structural checks pass; preserve IDs and repair\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-44-only the failed output if resumed.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-45-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-46-## Stop condition\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-47-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-48-Stop after two outputs. Do not select browser storage or claim the save gate is approved.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-49-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-50-## Acceptance criteria\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-51-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md:52:- R0005 and R0006 are the only generated contracts and match their two IMP allocations.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-53-- Both contracts retain the save/storage gate and make no incidental asset work.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md:54:- Loader, provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation completes before checkpointing.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md-55-- A mismatch stops rather than overwrites an R contract.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -C 8 'provenance|authoring_batch|source_specifications|asset_brief|R0005|manifest' scripts/runbookgen_status.py README.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nREADME.md-128-\nREADME.md-129-### Runbooks you normally use\nREADME.md-130-\nREADME.md-131-| Series | Meaning | Created by | Where it lives | What it does |\nREADME.md-132-| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\nREADME.md-133-| `INITIAL.md` | Source brief | You or `supervisor initial` | `projects/<project-name>/` | The concise source brief: what is being made, for whom, where it will run, constraints, references, and desired outcome. It gives every later stage its context. |\nREADME.md-134-| `F001`\u2013`F016` | **Factory** | This repository | `runbooks/` | **Factory runbooks.** They analyse the brief, write the detailed product plan, and create the files that will write the final implementation instructions. They do not build the requested product. |\nREADME.md-135-| `B0001`, `B0002`, \u2026 | **Bounded authoring batch** | The F-series and later B dispatcher files | `projects/<slug>/authoring-runbooks/` | **Runbook-writing tasks.** A B task writes the next small set of R files. \u201cBounded\u201d means it has a hard limit: one B task may write no more than seven R files. |\nREADME.md:136:| `R0001`, `R0002`, \u2026 | **Real product-work runbook** | B-series runbook-writing tasks | `projects/<slug>/runbooks/` | **Product-work runbooks.** Each R file gives detailed instructions and success checks for one small piece of building, testing, reviewing, documenting, or original-asset work. Every R file explicitly declares asset metadata and provenance links to its canonical specification, catalogue records, B batch, and originating F stages. |\nREADME.md-137-\nREADME.md-138-### Internal planning and coordination\nREADME.md-139-\nREADME.md-140-These files and records let the factory safely scale to a large application.\nREADME.md-141-They are important to the generator, but not things you normally need to read\nREADME.md-142-or manage while building the product.\nREADME.md-143-\nREADME.md-144-| Internal ID | Meaning | Created by | Where it lives | What it does |\nREADME.md-145-| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\nREADME.md-146-| `REQ-0001`, `REQ-0002`, \u2026 | **Functional requirement** | F011 specification/traceability stage | `projects/<slug>/specification/requirements.md`, `requirements.json`, and `traceability-matrix.md` | A stable statement of behaviour or capability the product must provide. It is a requirement, not a runnable task. |\nREADME.md-147-| `NFR-0001`, `NFR-0002`, \u2026 | **Non-functional requirement** | F011 specification/traceability stage | `projects/<slug>/specification/requirements.md`, `requirements.json`, and `traceability-matrix.md` | A stable quality or constraint requirement\u2014such as performance, accessibility, security, reliability, privacy, compatibility, or observability. It is not a runnable task. |\nREADME.md:148:| `IMP-0001`, `IMP-0002`, \u2026 | **Implementation catalogue record** | The F-series planning stages and later D dispatchers | `projects/<slug>/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` and the authoring manifest/ledger | **Planning and traceability records, not runnable runbooks.** Each record captures a needed piece of work, its requirements, dependencies, ownership, verification, and asset assessment before it is allocated to a B writer. |\nREADME.md:149:| `C0001`, `C0002`, \u2026 | **Catalogue checkpoint** | The factory or an authoring dispatcher | `projects/<slug>/authoring-runbooks/` | **Authoring coordination only.** A C task validates the catalogue, manifest, IDs, dependency coverage, and batch limits before another writing wave proceeds. It creates no product code and normally creates no R files. |\nREADME.md-150-| `D0001`, `D0002`, \u2026 | **Dispatcher** | The factory or an earlier dispatcher | `projects/<slug>/authoring-runbooks/` | **Authoring coordination only.** A D task expands one eligible planning chapter, allocates the next bounded B batches, and leaves one successor dispatcher if more catalogue work remains. It does not build the product or write R implementation files itself. |\nREADME.md-151-\nREADME.md-152-### How the generated runbooks and records connect\nREADME.md-153-\nREADME.md-154-Solid arrows show files or records created by a stage. Dotted arrows show\nREADME.md-155-validation, scheduling, or traceability links rather than a task creating its\nREADME.md-156-source material.\nREADME.md-157-\n--\nREADME.md-175-    D[\"D0001\u2026\\ndispatchers\\nauthoring-runbooks/\"] -. \"expands one eligible chapter\\nand allocates a later wave\" .-> IMP\nREADME.md-176-    D --> B\nREADME.md-177-    D -. \"creates successor when needed\" .-> D\nREADME.md-178-\nREADME.md-179-    B --> R[\"R0001\u2026\\nproduct-work runbooks\\nrunbooks/\"]\nREADME.md-180-    R -. \"requirement_ids\" .-> REQ\nREADME.md-181-    R -. \"requirement_ids\" .-> NFR\nREADME.md-182-    R -. \"source_catalogue_ids\" .-> IMP\nREADME.md:183:    R -. \"source_specifications\" .-> SPEC\nREADME.md:184:    R -. \"authoring_batch\" .-> B\nREADME.md-185-```\nREADME.md-186-\nREADME.md-187-In short:\nREADME.md-188-\nREADME.md-189-```text\nREADME.md-190-your brief \u2192 F-series factory \u2192 B-series runbook writers \u2192 R-series product work\nREADME.md-191-                                  \u2191 C checkpoints and D dispatchers coordinate authoring only\nREADME.md-192-```\n--\nREADME.md-224-available for targeted lookup.\nREADME.md-225-\nREADME.md-226-| When | What is used | Why |\nREADME.md-227-| --- | --- | --- |\nREADME.md-228-| `F001` | `projects/<name>/INITIAL.md` | The user\u2019s original brief is the source of truth. F001 normalizes it but never replaces it. |\nREADME.md-229-| `F002`\u2013`F004` | `INITIAL.md`, `PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, and the relevant earlier specification chapters | These stages refine product/domain, technical, and experience decisions. They use the documents produced by earlier F stages\u2014not every earlier F Markdown procedure. |\nREADME.md-230-| `F005`\u2013`F010` | The canonical `specification/` chapters and earlier planning outputs | These stages translate established decisions into dependencies, delivery areas, authoring contracts, and a safe handoff. |\nREADME.md-231-| `F011`\u2013`F013` | The canonical specification plus the delivery/contract planning outputs | These stages create the traceability system, implementation catalogue, dependency graph, and small B-series batches. |\nREADME.md:232:| `F014`\u2013`F016` | The catalogue, authoring manifest, quality gate, and canonical specification | These stages create B writers, validate their intended R contracts, register the B child collection, and publish the R handoff for a separate implementation supervisor. |\nREADME.md-233-| A B-series writer | Its own F013 context packet: only the assigned catalogue records, relevant specification sections, target constraints, templates, and reserved IDs | It writes no more than seven R files without needing a huge prompt or unrelated product context. |\nREADME.md:234:| A C checkpoint or D dispatcher | The authoring manifest, catalogue, ledger, and only the relevant canonical specification chapter | It validates and schedules the authoring process; it is not product implementation context. |\nREADME.md:235:| An R-series task | Its own objective, dependencies, acceptance criteria, and provenance metadata | It performs one small piece of product work. It can open the linked canonical files when it needs more detail. |\nREADME.md-236-\nREADME.md:237:Each generated R file must declare this provenance in its front matter:\nREADME.md-238-\nREADME.md-239-```yaml\nREADME.md-240-requirement_ids:\nREADME.md-241-  - REQ-0007\nREADME.md-242-  - NFR-0004\nREADME.md:243:source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#save-state\nREADME.md-244-source_catalogue_ids: IMP-SAVE-001\nREADME.md:245:authoring_batch: B0007\nREADME.md-246-factory_stages: F003,F005,F012,F013\nREADME.md-247-```\nREADME.md-248-\nREADME.md-249-These fields answer different questions:\nREADME.md-250-\nREADME.md-251-- `requirement_ids` \u2014 which functional (`REQ-*`) and quality/constraint (`NFR-*`) requirements the task fulfils or verifies.\nREADME.md:252:- `source_specifications` \u2014 which canonical requirement sections explain the work.\nREADME.md-253-- `source_catalogue_ids` \u2014 which planned implementation records the task covers.\nREADME.md:254:- `authoring_batch` \u2014 which bounded B writer created this R task.\nREADME.md-255-- `factory_stages` \u2014 which F stages established the underlying requirement.\nREADME.md-256-\nREADME.md:257:The F and B references provide **provenance**, not a reason to use procedural\nREADME.md-258-factory Markdown as implementation requirements. The canonical specification\nREADME.md-259-and planning files remain the authoritative context. R-to-R dependencies define\nREADME.md-260-execution order; this factory follows an explicit `.supervisor-children/`\nREADME.md-261-registration from the F collection to the B collection only. The resulting R\nREADME.md-262-collection is deliberately left for the separate implementation supervisor.\nREADME.md-263-\nREADME.md-264-After every B-series authoring wave, run that project's structural quality gate\nREADME.md-265-(for example, `python3 projects/<project-name>/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py`).\nREADME.md:266:It checks authoring provenance, ownership, assets, browser-test reservations,\nREADME.md-267-and coverage; it is not evidence of product implementation, testing, or release\nREADME.md-268-readiness.\nREADME.md-269-\nREADME.md-270-### Terms used in this repository\nREADME.md-271-\nREADME.md-272-| Term | Meaning here |\nREADME.md-273-| --- | --- |\nREADME.md-274-| **Runbook** | A Markdown work instruction with scope, steps, dependencies, and evidence required to mark it complete. |\nREADME.md-275-| **Runbook-writing task / authoring task** | A runbook whose output is more runbook Markdown files. It does not write application code. B-series files write R files; C/D-series files coordinate the authoring process. |\nREADME.md-276-| **Bounded** | Deliberately limited in size. A B-series task writes a maximum of seven R-series files. |\nREADME.md-277-| **Functional requirement (`REQ-*`)** | A stable statement of behaviour or capability the product must provide. Stored in the project\u2019s `specification/requirements.md` and `requirements.json`, with coverage shown in `traceability-matrix.md`. |\nREADME.md-278-| **Non-functional requirement (`NFR-*`)** | A stable quality, safety, delivery, or operating constraint\u2014such as performance, accessibility, security, reliability, privacy, or compatibility. Stored and traced alongside functional requirements. |\nREADME.md-279-| **Catalogue** | The complete checklist of product work that must eventually be covered: features, technical foundations, content, quality, release work, and dependencies. |\nREADME.md:280:| **Implementation catalogue record (`IMP-*`)** | One stable planned work record in `planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` and the authoring manifest/ledger. It is allocated to an authoring batch before one or more R-series runbooks are written. It is not itself runnable. |\nREADME.md-281-| **Collection** | A folder of runbooks that Supervisor can run. The root F collection creates child B and R collections for one generated project. |\nREADME.md-282-| **Catalogue checkpoint (C)** | An internal authoring control that checks the catalogue and allocation ledger before a new writing wave can proceed. It creates no application deliverable. |\nREADME.md-283-| **Dispatcher (D)** | An internal authoring control that creates the next bounded B-series files when more parts of the catalogue still need R runbooks. It creates no application deliverable. |\nREADME.md-284-| **Contract** | The required shape of a runbook: its goal, inputs, steps, acceptance criteria, and evidence. It is not a legal agreement or an API contract. |\nREADME.md-285-\nREADME.md-286-### F-series factory stages, in detail\nREADME.md-287-\nREADME.md-288-The F-series is deliberately product-agnostic. It uses the brief to decide what\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc 'python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py' in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nRunbook-generation structural quality gate (not product/release evidence)\ncanonical specification chapters: 13\nspecification provenance links: 22\ncatalogue contracts: 12 (IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0004, IMP-0005, IMP-0006, IMP-0007, IMP-0008, IMP-0009, IMP-0010, IMP-0011, IMP-0012)\nmanifest contracts: 12 (R0001, R0002, R0003, R0004, R0005, R0006, R0007, R0008, R0009, R0010, R0011, R0012)\nR files missing: 0\nblocked contracts: 0\nunverified contracts: 0\nunallocated catalogue contracts: 0\nreserved asset IDs: 0\nbrowser test paths: 0\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py\nsed -n '1,220p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\nsed -n '1,160p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Structural quality gate for generated B-series and R-series runbooks.\n\nThis validates planning artefacts only; it is never product or release evidence.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nREPOSITORY = ROOT.parents[1]\nMANIFEST_PATH = ROOT / \"planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"\nCATALOGUE_PATH = ROOT / \"planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\"\nR_ID, F_ID = re.compile(r\"^R\\d{4}$\"), re.compile(r\"^F\\d{3}$\")\nLIST_FIELDS = {\n    \"dependencies\", \"requirement_ids\", \"source_specifications\",\n    \"source_catalogue_ids\", \"factory_stages\", \"asset_ids\", \"audio_ids\",\n    \"playwright_spec\", \"playwright_specs\",\n}\n\ndef values(value):\n    return value if isinstance(value, list) else ([value] if value else [])\n\ndef parse_value(value):\n    value = value.strip().strip(\"\\\"'\")\n    if value == \"[]\": return []\n    if value.startswith(\"[\") and value.endswith(\"]\"):\n        return [item.strip().strip(\"\\\"'\") for item in value[1:-1].split(\",\") if item.strip()]\n    return value\n\ndef front_matter(path):\n    text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    if not text.startswith(\"---\\n\"): return {}\n    end = text.find(\"\\n---\", 4)\n    if end < 0: return {}\n    result, key = {}, None\n    for line in text[4:end].splitlines():\n        if line.lstrip().startswith(\"-\") and key:\n            result.setdefault(key, []).append(parse_value(line.split(\"-\", 1)[1]))\n        elif \":\" in line:\n            key, value = line.split(\":\", 1); key = key.strip(); value = parse_value(value)\n            # Authoring runbooks use compact comma-delimited metadata for\n            # these schema-defined lists. Preserve scalar prose fields such as\n            # asset_brief verbatim while normalising only list metadata.\n            result[key] = [item.strip() for item in value.split(\",\") if item.strip()] if key in LIST_FIELDS and isinstance(value, str) else value\n    return result\n\ndef headings(path):\n    return {re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"-\", match.group(1).lower()).strip(\"-\")\n            for match in re.finditer(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+?)\\s*$\", path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"), re.M)}\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--wave\", help=\"validate allocations through this B batch\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    manifest = json.loads(MANIFEST_PATH.read_text())\n    catalogue = json.loads(CATALOGUE_PATH.read_text())\n    batches = {b[\"id\"]: b for b in manifest[\"batches\"]}\n    contracts = manifest[\"r_contracts\"]\n    if args.wave:\n        if args.wave not in batches: parser.error(\"unknown B batch: \" + args.wave)\n        contracts = [c for c in contracts if batches.get(c.get(\"authoring_batch\"), {}).get(\"order\", 999) <= batches[args.wave][\"order\"]]\n    records = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in catalogue[\"contracts\"]}\n    errors, missing, blocked, unverified = [], [], [], []\n    def fail(text): errors.append(text)\n    ids = [c.get(\"id\", \"\") for c in contracts]\n    if ids != sorted(ids): fail(\"manifest R IDs are not sequence ordered\")\n    for item, count in Counter(ids).items():\n        if count > 1: fail(\"duplicate manifest R ID \" + item)\n    paths = [c.get(\"output_path\", \"\") for c in contracts]\n    for item, count in Counter(paths).items():\n        if count > 1: fail(\"duplicate output path \" + item)\n    assets, browser_paths = {}, defaultdict(list)\n    # The authoring collection is part of the gate: each allocated batch must\n    # exist, identify itself, and be the sole owner of its manifest R IDs.\n    for batch_id, batch_record in batches.items():\n        batch_path = ROOT / \"authoring-runbooks\" / f\"{batch_id}.md\"\n        meta = front_matter(batch_path) if batch_path.is_file() else {}\n        if not meta: fail(f\"{batch_id}: missing or invalid B-series front matter\")\n        elif meta.get(\"task_id\") != batch_id: fail(f\"{batch_id}: task ID mismatch in authoring runbook\")\n        if len(batch_record.get(\"r_contract_ids\", [])) > 7: fail(f\"{batch_id}: exceeds seven-contract batch limit\")\n    for contract in contracts:\n        rid, batch = contract.get(\"id\", \"\"), contract.get(\"authoring_batch\", \"\")\n        if not R_ID.fullmatch(rid): fail(f\"invalid R ID {rid!r}\")\n        if batch not in batches or rid not in batches.get(batch, {}).get(\"r_contract_ids\", []): fail(f\"{rid}: authoring batch ownership mismatch\")\n        catalogue_ids = values(contract.get(\"source_catalogue_ids\"))\n        if not catalogue_ids or contract.get(\"catalogue_id\") not in catalogue_ids: fail(f\"{rid}: missing or inconsistent catalogue provenance\")\n        for cid in catalogue_ids:\n            if cid not in records: fail(f\"{rid}: unknown catalogue ID {cid}\")\n        if contract.get(\"catalogue_id\") in records and not records[contract[\"catalogue_id\"]].get(\"requirement_ids\"): fail(f\"{rid}: catalogue record lacks requirement links\")\n        specs = values(contract.get(\"source_specifications\"))\n        if not specs: fail(f\"{rid}: missing source_specifications\")\n        for link in specs:\n            file_name, _, anchor = link.partition(\"#\"); source = ROOT / file_name\n            if not link.startswith(\"specification/\") or not source.is_file() or (anchor and anchor not in headings(source)):\n                fail(f\"{rid}: unresolved canonical specification link {link}\")\n        stages = values(contract.get(\"factory_stages\"))\n        if not stages or any(not F_ID.fullmatch(s) for s in stages): fail(f\"{rid}: invalid factory_stages\")\n        for dependency in values(contract.get(\"dependencies\")):\n            if dependency not in ids: fail(f\"{rid}: dependency {dependency} is outside allocation\")\n            elif dependency >= rid: fail(f\"{rid}: dependency {dependency} does not precede contract\")\n        impact, asset_ids = contract.get(\"asset_impact\"), values(contract.get(\"asset_ids\"))\n        if impact not in {\"required\", \"not_applicable\"}: fail(f\"{rid}: invalid asset_impact\")\n        if \"asset_ids\" not in contract: fail(f\"{rid}: asset_ids absent\")\n        if impact == \"required\":\n            if not asset_ids or not contract.get(\"asset_brief\") or not contract.get(\"visual_style_version\"): fail(f\"{rid}: required assets lack IDs, brief, or style version\")\n            for asset in asset_ids:\n                if not re.fullmatch(r\"ASSET-[A-Z0-9-]+\", asset): fail(f\"{rid}: unstable asset ID {asset}\")\n                if asset in assets: fail(f\"asset {asset} ambiguously owned by {assets[asset]} and {rid}\")\n                assets[asset] = rid\n        elif asset_ids: fail(f\"{rid}: non-asset contract reserves asset IDs\")\n        if batches.get(batch, {}).get(\"state\") in {\"blocked_on_gate\", \"blocked\", \"repairable\"}: blocked.append(rid)\n        r_path = REPOSITORY / contract.get(\"output_path\", \"\")\n        if not r_path.is_file(): missing.append(rid); continue\n        meta = front_matter(r_path)\n        for field in (\"task_id\", \"sequence\", \"source_specifications\", \"source_catalogue_ids\", \"authoring_batch\", \"factory_stages\", \"asset_impact\", \"asset_ids\"):\n            if field not in meta: fail(f\"{rid}: {r_path.name} lacks {field}\")\n        if \"requirement_ids\" not in meta: fail(f\"{rid}: {r_path.name} lacks requirement_ids\")\n        if meta.get(\"task_id\") != rid: fail(f\"{rid}: task ID mismatch\")\n        if values(meta.get(\"requirement_ids\")) != records.get(contract.get(\"catalogue_id\"), {}).get(\"requirement_ids\", []): fail(f\"{rid}: requirement_ids differ from catalogue\")\n        for field in (\"source_specifications\", \"source_catalogue_ids\", \"authoring_batch\", \"factory_stages\", \"asset_impact\", \"asset_ids\"):\n            if values(meta.get(field)) != values(contract.get(field)): fail(f\"{rid}: {field} differs from manifest\")\n        browser, specs = meta.get(\"browser_impact\", \"not_applicable\"), values(meta.get(\"playwright_spec\", meta.get(\"playwright_specs\")))\n        if browser == \"not_applicable\" and specs: fail(f\"{rid}: browser path on non-browser contract\")\n        if browser != \"not_applicable\" and (not specs or not set(records.get(contract.get(\"catalogue_id\"), {}).get(\"targets\", [])) & {\"web\", \"pwa\"}): fail(f\"{rid}: browser metadata outside browser behaviour scope\")\n        for spec in specs: browser_paths[spec].append(rid)\n        body = r_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        if \"## Verification\" not in body: unverified.append(rid)\n        if not re.search(r\"^## Asset assessment\\s*$\", body, re.M | re.I): fail(f\"{rid}: missing explicit Asset assessment section\")\n    for path, owners in browser_paths.items():\n        if len(owners) > 1: fail(f\"duplicate browser test path {path}: {', '.join(owners)}\")\n    graph = {c[\"id\"]: values(c.get(\"dependencies\")) for c in contracts}; active, done = set(), set()\n    def visit(node):\n        if node in active: fail(\"unsupported circular dependency through \" + node); return\n        if node not in done:\n            active.add(node)\n            for dep in graph[node]:\n                if dep in graph: visit(dep)\n            active.remove(node); done.add(node)\n    for node in graph: visit(node)\n    # Discovered families need a canonical source and a category-appropriate\n    # catalogue/verification route. Explicitly held connected scope is a valid\n    # reviewed outcome, not a missing P0 implementation contract.\n    review = ROOT / \"specification/domain-completeness-review.md\"\n    for line in review.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n        if not line.startswith(\"|\") or line.startswith(\"| System\") or line.startswith(\"| ---\"): continue\n        cells = [cell.strip() for cell in line.split(\"|\")[1:-1]]\n        if len(cells) != 5: continue\n        family, source, _deps, authoring, decision = cells\n        if \"SPEC-\" not in source: fail(f\"domain family {family}: no specification chapter\")\n        if \"hold\" in decision.lower(): continue\n        keywords = [word.lower() for word in re.findall(r\"[A-Za-z]{5,}\", family)]\n        searchable = json.dumps(catalogue).lower()\n        if not any(word in searchable for word in keywords): fail(f\"domain family {family}: no catalogue traceability\")\n        if authoring.lower() not in {\"none\", \"n/a\"} and not authoring: fail(f\"domain family {family}: no content/authoring approach\")\n    allocated = {c.get(\"catalogue_id\") for c in contracts}\n    unallocated = [cid for cid in records if cid not in allocated]\n    print(\"Runbook-generation structural quality gate (not product/release evidence)\")\n    chapter_count = len(list((ROOT / \"specification\").glob(\"*.md\")))\n    source_link_count = sum(len(values(c.get(\"source_specifications\"))) for c in contracts)\n    print(f\"canonical specification chapters: {chapter_count}\")\n    print(f\"specification provenance links: {source_link_count}\")\n    for label, result in ((\"catalogue contracts\", list(records)), (\"manifest contracts\", ids), (\"R files missing\", missing), (\"blocked contracts\", blocked), (\"unverified contracts\", unverified), (\"unallocated catalogue contracts\", unallocated), (\"reserved asset IDs\", list(assets)), (\"browser test paths\", list(browser_paths))):\n        print(f\"{label}: {len(result)}\" + (\" (\" + \", \".join(sorted(result)) + \")\" if result else \"\"))\n    for error in errors: print(\"ERROR:\", error)\n    return 1 if errors or missing or unverified else 0\nif __name__ == \"__main__\": sys.exit(main())\n---\ntask_id: B0004\nsequence: 5\ntitle: Author content-validation and local recovery contracts\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nAfter B0003, create only `../runbooks/R0005.md` and `../runbooks/R0006.md`\nfor IMP-0005 and IMP-0006; retain GATE-0003.\n\n## Context packet\n\nRead the B0004/R0005/R0006 manifest records, the two catalogue records,\n`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas`,\n`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n`02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence`, and\n`04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states`.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `../runbooks/R0005.md` \u2014 IMP-0005; dependencies R0001,R0003,R0004.\n- `../runbooks/R0006.md` \u2014 IMP-0006; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0004.\n\n## Required authoring content\n\nUse standard front matter, exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch: B0004`),\nand `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank `asset_ids`. Each output must\ncover objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership, behaviour, non-goals,\nplatform differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria,\nand an `## Asset assessment` forbidding incidental asset creation.\n\n## Validation procedure\n\nNever overwrite a conflicting R file. Load and compare both files with the\nmanifest, including provenance and dependencies, then verify required sections\nand GATE-0003 retention.\n\n## Checkpoint and update procedure\n\nUpdate B0004 only after both structural checks pass; preserve IDs and repair\nonly the failed output if resumed.\n\n## Stop condition\n\nStop after two outputs. Do not select browser storage or claim the save gate is approved.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- R0005 and R0006 are the only generated contracts and match their two IMP allocations.\n- Both contracts retain the save/storage gate and make no incidental asset work.\n- Loader, provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation completes before checkpointing.\n- A mismatch stops rather than overwrites an R contract.\n# Implementation-runbook authoring context\n\nThis collection creates implementation instructions only. The canonical project\nscope is [PROJECT_BRIEF.md](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md); read the canonical\n[specification](../specification/README.md) and the allocation ledger at\n[`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json)\nbefore writing an R-series file. Do not infer, approve, or implement unresolved\ndecisions. This collection is a child of the factory collection and its R-series\noutput is registered as its own child collection.\n\nThe initial wave is deliberately limited to the already allocated SHARD-01\nfoundation contracts. Future work is created only by the dispatcher, one\ncatalogue chapter and at most ten B-series tasks at a time.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,42p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\nsed -n '1,55p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\nsed -n '1,80p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n{\n  \"catalogue_id\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4-implementation-catalogue\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"source\": [\"../specification/README.md\", \"../specification/requirements.json\", \"05-delivery-map.md\", \"06-foundation-domain-contracts.md\", \"07-feature-experience-contracts.md\", \"08-quality-operations-contracts.md\"],\n  \"scope\": \"P0 is an original, offline-capable 2D single-player fantasy RPG delivered through a shared web core and a PWA delivery adaptation. Connected services are not P0 implementation scope.\",\n  \"first_bounded_domain\": {\"id\": \"SHARD-01\", \"title\": \"Foundation and core contracts\", \"contract_limit\": 250, \"contract_count\": 12, \"state\": \"ready_for_authoring\", \"boundary\": \"Framework-neutral seams, deterministic state/data contracts, local persistence protocol, quality foundations, and original-design controls; excludes campaign rules, UI flows, PWA lifecycle, and release execution.\"},\n  \"contracts\": [\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0001\",\"title\":\"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\",\"domain\":\"foundation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A framework-neutral project skeleton documents one bootstrap, lint, format, and deterministic test command with isolated shared, web-adapter, PWA-adapter, content, and test directories.\",\"prerequisites\":[],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"root build/tooling configuration\",\"src/{core,content,app,platform/web,platform/pwa}/\",\"tests/\",\"docs/development.md\"],\"data\":[\"pinned toolchain declaration\"],\"api\":[\"build/test command interface\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"selecting framework/package manager/CI without DEC-0001\",\"gameplay\",\"service worker\",\"hosting\"],\"verification\":\"Clean approved-runtime checkout runs the documented deterministic sample test, lint, and format checks.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 framework, package-manager, and CI selection before implementation.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0002\",\"title\":\"Enforce shared-core and adapter dependency seams\",\"domain\":\"foundation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"REQ-0013\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A dependency policy and public interfaces prevent core code from importing browser, renderer, clock, network, or platform modules; adapters submit commands and render returned state/events.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/public interfaces\",\"src/platform/{web,pwa}/adapter interfaces\",\"architecture dependency rules\",\"docs/architecture.md\"],\"data\":[\"dependency-policy manifest\"],\"api\":[\"Command, state, event, and adapter interfaces\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"concrete combat/exploration/UI\",\"account or network client\",\"target-specific campaign rules\"],\"verification\":\"A dependency-rule test rejects forbidden core imports and a fixture adapter proves command-only interaction.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"None; retain GATE-0001 for tool-specific enforcement.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0003\",\"title\":\"Create deterministic test and fixture harness\",\"domain\":\"tests\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Layered unit, content, integration, and reserved browser-test conventions provide isolated RNG/clock and persistence fixtures with no real service or player data access.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"test-runner configuration\",\"tests/{core,content,platform,app}/fixtures\",\"docs/testing.md\"],\"data\":[\"deterministic fixture factories\"],\"api\":[\"test fixture and fake clock/RNG interfaces\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"final feature assertions\",\"real browser/device matrix claims\",\"production telemetry\"],\"verification\":\"Repeated core fixture execution has identical results; a deliberately failing fixture is detected; fixture storage is isolated.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 before compatibility or performance claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0004\",\"title\":\"Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\",\"domain\":\"data\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0003\",\"REQ-0004\",\"REQ-0006\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0010\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Immutable versioned state, command/result/event envelopes, revision and interaction identifiers, deterministic RNG state, and invariant helpers define legal transition mechanics without feature state machines.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}/\",\"tests/core/contract.*\"],\"data\":[\"campaign snapshot envelope\",\"deterministic RNG state\"],\"api\":[\"Core command/state/event API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"authored values\",\"combat/inventory/quest algorithms\",\"save driver\",\"UI selection state\",\"account/network state\"],\"verification\":\"Invalid and stale commands do not mutate state; duplicate interaction IDs cause no extra durable transition.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 before concrete party/content shapes.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"domain\":\"content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0007\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Typed content-package schema and validator cover IDs, references, locale keys, assets, predicates, rewards, and reachability but contain no authored campaign expression.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/content/{schema,validator,registry}/\",\"tests/content/validation.*\",\"docs/content-authoring.md\"],\"data\":[\"versioned content package format\",\"asset/provenance manifest schema\"],\"api\":[\"content registry and validator API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"town/dungeon dialogue/maps/assets\",\"copied reference expression\",\"release packaging\"],\"verification\":\"Valid minimum package passes; each invalid reference class fails; a graph fixture checks opening-to-ending reachability.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 for quantities, locale, and content detail; human provenance review remains required.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0006\",\"title\":\"Specify local save and recovery protocol\",\"domain\":\"persistence\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0006\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0005\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A schema protocol specifies immutable revisions, checksums, current-pointer validation, known-good retention, quarantine, separate preferences, deletion confirmation, and safe-boundary persistence rules.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/save/{schema,compatibility,migrations}/\",\"src/platform/web/persistence/\",\"tests/{core,platform}/save*\",\"docs/save-and-recovery.md\"],\"data\":[\"save snapshot and preference schemas\",\"quarantine record\"],\"api\":[\"snapshot repository and recovery protocol\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"cloud sync\",\"identity\",\"PWA cache records\",\"eviction guarantee\"],\"verification\":\"Fault fixtures cover interrupted write, checksum failure, malformed data, quota/permission failure, quarantine, retry, and selected-slot deletion.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 storage API, quota, support window, and recovery policy.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0007\",\"title\":\"Define pure save migration runner\",\"domain\":\"persistence\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0006\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Ordered, pure migrations declare supported versions and promote only validated candidates while preserving original invalid bytes for quarantine.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/save/{migrations,compatibility}/\",\"tests/core/save/fixtures\"],\"data\":[\"migration registry and predecessor fixtures\"],\"api\":[\"migration runner API\"]},\"