-01\"],\"covers\":[\"identity/sync conflict policy\",\"multiplayer/player safety\",\"live operations\",\"commerce/entitlements\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0014\",\"REQ-0015\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0006\",\"target_allocation\":\"no P0 target implementation; research/decision outputs only if explicitly authorised\",\"state\":\"hold\"}\n  ],\n  \"requirement_coverage\": {\n    \"REQ-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-02; provenance foundation IMP-0011\",\"REQ-0002\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0003\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0004\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0005\":\"queued: SHARD-02 and SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0007\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0009\":\"queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0010\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0011\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0013\":\"current: IMP-0002, IMP-0008\",\"REQ-0014\":\"gated: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"REQ-0015\":\"hold: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"NFR-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0002\":\"current/gated: IMP-0004, IMP-0006, IMP-0007\",\"NFR-0003\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0004\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0005\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0007\":\"current: IMP-0005; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0010, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0009\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0002\",\"NFR-0010\":\"current: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0004; queued target adapters in SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0011\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0005\",\"NFR-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0008, IMP-0012; queued: SHARD-04\"\n  },\n  \"dependency_graph\": {\"nodes\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0008\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0010\",\"IMP-0011\",\"IMP-0012\"],\"acyclic\":true,\"validation\":\"Each prerequisite points only to an earlier numbered contract; SHARD dependencies only point from later shards to earlier shards.\"}\n}\n---\ntask_id: R0005\nsequence: 5\ntitle: Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\ndependencies: R0001,R0003,R0004\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas,specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0005\nauthoring_batch: B0004\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No art or audio assets; reserve schema and provenance fields only for later original assets.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDefine the shared, versioned content-package schema, read-only registry, and\nvalidator that reject malformed or internally inconsistent content before it\ncan be loaded for play. The contract validates structure and relationships;\nit does not author a town, dungeon, dialogue, map, encounter, or other campaign\nexpression.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0001 provides the project boundary, R0003 provides deterministic fixtures,\nand R0004 provides versioned campaign-state envelopes. They are implementation\ndependencies, not authoring blockers. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003: save storage\nAPI, quota, support-window, and recovery policy decisions remain owned by the\nlocal-save protocol. This content contract neither chooses nor writes a save or\ncache implementation.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `src/content/{schema,validator,registry}/`.\n- `tests/content/validation.*` and deterministic content graph fixtures.\n- `docs/content-authoring.md`.\n- The versioned content-package, asset/provenance-manifest, and validator API\n  contracts.\n\nThe content registry loads only a fully validated package and is read-only at\nruntime. It does not own campaign state, save snapshots, preferences, browser\nstorage, PWA cache records, migrations, assets, or release packaging.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nModel a package with stable package ID, semantic version, schema version,\n---\ntask_id: R0001\nsequence: 1\ntitle: Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\ndependencies:\nrequirement_ids: NFR-0010,NFR-0012\nsource_specifications: specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition,specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001\nauthoring_batch: B0001\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No product asset work; establish only project/tooling boundaries and prohibit incidental assets.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nAfter DEC-0001 selects the framework, package manager, and CI baseline, create\nthe smallest reproducible project skeleton for the shared game core, web\nadapter, and PWA adapter. Document one bootstrap, format, lint, and\ndeterministic test command interface, and make a clean approved-runtime\ncheckout run a deterministic sample test. This task establishes boundaries and\ntooling only; it does not implement game behaviour or resolve the decision.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThis is the first implementation contract and has no R-series dependencies.\nGATE-0001 / DEC-0001 is retained as a human implementation precondition:\nauthoring this runbook does not select a stack, and implementation must stop\nbefore selecting or installing framework, package-manager, or CI tooling.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- Root build and tooling configuration, including the pinned toolchain\n  declaration and command mapping.\n- `src/core/`, `src/content/`, `src/app/`, `src/platform/web/`, and\n  `src/platform/pwa/` ownership directories, created without feature code.\n- `tests/` and an isolated deterministic sample-test location.\n- `docs/development.md`, which records the approved-runtime bootstrap,\n  format, lint, and deterministic-test commands once DEC-0001 is decided.\n- The build/test command interface: `bootstrap`, `format`, `lint`, and\n  `test:deterministic` (or the selected tool's documented equivalent).\n\n## Behaviour\n\nUse the DEC-0001-approved runtime only. Pin its version and package-manager\nlock/metadata as appropriate to that approved selection. Create the isolated\ndirectory skeleton so later work has distinct shared-core, content, app,\nweb-adapter, PWA-adapter, and test ownership.\n\nConfigure the selected tooling so the documented command interface has a\nsingle reproducible mapping for bootstrap, formatting, linting, and a\ndeterministic sample test. The sample test must use no wall clock, network,\nplayer data, browser storage, renderer, or platform feature. Record the exact\ncommands and a clean-checkout result in `docs/development.md`.\n\nThe skeleton must preserve the canonical direction: target adapters are\nseparate from the shared deterministic core, and no directory implies that a\ntarget may change campaign rules. Later R0002 owns enforcement of detailed\ncore/adapter dependency rules.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nThe responsive web and installable PWA targets receive separate adapter\ndirectories only. Neither adapter gains a renderer, service worker, cache\nlifecycle, browser API dependency, or target-specific campaign behaviour in\nthis task. PWA installation, caching, offline delivery, and update activation\nremain later scoped work; the PWA directory is an ownership boundary, not an\nimplementation of those features.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -C 3 'R0005|B0004|mock-fantasy-quest-4|accepted|provenance' runbooks/.supervisor-children supervisor projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4 -g '*.json' -g '*.md' -g '*.yml' -g '*.yaml' | sed -n '1,360p'\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nrunbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json:1:{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\"}\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md:1:# mock-fantasy-quest-4 runbook factory handoff\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-2-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-3-This workspace is a **planning and runbook-authoring factory** for an eventual\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-4-implementation project. It does not contain a game implementation, product\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-44-story/lore, dialogue, maps, art, music, layouts, combat screens, or distinctive\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-45-interaction choreography. All creative work must be independently original and\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-46-follow the warm hand-painted, readable-silhouette, restrained-palette direction\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md:47:with provenance and human creative review.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-48-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-49-## Run the factory and authoring collections\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-50-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md:51:Run these from the repository root. `--project mock-fantasy-quest-4` loads this\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-52-workspace's versioned, non-secret Supervisor configuration and uses its durable\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md:53:state. An accepted task is skipped on a later collection run unless explicitly\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-54-retried.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-55-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md-56-### 1. Factory collection