/D0001.md-45-allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md:46:rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-47-dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-48-queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-49-B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-53-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-54-Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-55-files, no more than seven assigned R IDs per B file, unique B/R/IMP IDs,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md:56:dependency closure, provenance values, asset metadata, output ownership, and\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-57-the successor/final-audit choice. Stop and report a source conflict, missing\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-58-coverage, cycle, ID/path collision, unresolved authority, or any need to\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md:59:overwrite accepted work.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-60-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-61-## Stop condition\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-62-\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-70-- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md-71-- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, che